---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy — Zero Company Field Guide" description="Privacy information for Zero Company Field Guide." path="/privacy/" noindex={true}>
  <article class="shell legal">
    <p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY NOTICE</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>Optional Google Analytics 4 measurement is denied by default and loads only after you choose “Allow analytics.” It helps us understand aggregate page visits, navigation choices, and which guide sections are useful.</p>
    <p>Advertising storage, ad user data, ad personalization, Google signals, and remarketing remain disabled. Your analytics choice is stored locally in your browser. You can reject, withdraw, or reopen the choice at any time using “Analytics choices” in the footer.</p>
    <h2>Third-party advertising</h2>
    <p>This site loads a third-party native advertising script from <code>profitableratecpmnetwork.com</code> on site pages, including this Privacy page. That request is separate from optional Google Analytics.</p>
    <p>When the advertising script runs, the provider and its ad-serving partners may receive technical request data such as your IP address, browser or device information, and page or referrer context. They may use cookies, pixels, or similar technologies to deliver and measure ads, prevent fraud, and personalize advertising, subject to their own policies. See <a href="https://adsterra.com/cookies/" rel="noreferrer">Adsterra's cookies policy</a>.</p>
    <p>“Analytics choices” controls only optional Google Analytics. It does not block or withdraw the third-party advertising request. This site does not currently provide a separate advertising choice.</p>
    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>Links to Electronic Arts and YouTube leave this local guide. The embedded official trailer uses YouTube's privacy-enhanced domain, but loading or playing it may still connect your browser to YouTube. Those services apply their own privacy practices.</p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is delivered through Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare may process technical request data required to serve and protect the website under its own privacy terms.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.legal{max-width:780px;padding:4rem 0}.legal h1{font-size:clamp(2.7rem,7vw,5rem)}.legal h2{margin-top:2.2rem}.legal p{color:var(--muted-strong)}</style>
